id: pm-preview-path-refusal
title: Declare non-regular transaction preview paths as recoverable SDK refusals
description: Sentry PM-CLI-3E reports a handled Windows transaction preview refusal as unclassified_runtime_error with exit 1 on installed 2026.10.6. Preserve non-following filesystem safety while emitting a declared path-redacted refusal and actionable repair guidance from SDK producers and opened descriptor checks.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-07T05:16:46.951Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-07T06:17:11.978Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-07T06:16:17.392Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-07T06:16:17.392Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Real symlink and directory controls reach declared refusal;SDK and CLI preserve source bytes and expose actionable bounded recovery;Opened-descriptor refusal follows the same typed contract;Generated catalog classifies current handled events without message allowlists;Exact all-source coverage and mandatory checks remain intact
parent: pm-3lhth4
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Use declared transaction_preview_non_regular_file PmCliError at entry and descriptor checks with usage exit 2 and bounded repair guidance; retain non-following safety and native errno diagnostics, regenerate SDK and runtime error surfaces."
expected_result: Non-regular preview storage fails closed through the SDK and CLI with stable code actionable recovery and unchanged source bytes.
actual_result: "78 linked preview controls plus installed Node/Bun acceptance pass; real links FIFOs sockets directories and descriptor races are covered. Exact all-source 100/100/100/100 coverage, static and four TypeScript projects pass. Sentry resolution is reserved for the next release containing the validated source fix."
